/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180191#post180191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw shit, Destroyers got the Want It, Need It spell. Game over man, game over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which? Apple of Discord or one of the other Cacophony Embeds?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180233#post180233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well now I gotta have a look at that.<br /> <br /> First off, thank you all for Stop, and second, Terrible Avatar is the perfect offset to my first demon character's first key of Alibi, with the general struggle of wanting it both ways(a simple human life and a violent lobotomy of the God-Machine) so really thank you for that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Omigosh, the Gadget chapter has so many things I've been thinking about for so long. <i>Onyx Path can read my mind</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrible Avatar was fun. For when you absolutely have to wreck shit but don't want the hunter angels to get all up in your face while you do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T19:20:06-07:00","id":180271,"title":"","content":"Apple of Discord. TO be fair the myth came before My Little Pony did it, but I can't think of someone <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fX5nDlafVEc\" target=\"_blank\">doing a song</a> to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T19:22:15-07:00","id":180273,"title":"","content":"I just finished the opening fiction.<br /> <br /> It was probably one of the greatest RPG introductory pieces I've seen so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T22:19:51-07:00","id":180444,"title":"","content":"This thread is surprisingly not exploding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T22:22:19-07:00","id":180445,"title":"","content":"Unlike <i>Heirs</i> everyone needs to buy this one instead of getting it for free. As such I'm sure there's several people waiting for paychecks to clear/some money to come by that'll facilitate their purchase.<br /> <br /> I'm still readin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T22:36:23-07:00","id":180451,"title":"","content":"Can't get it until friday - nothing quite like having 60 cents in the old bank account, eh? - but cannot wait. Hope my Integrator babies get the love they deserve and the Stigmatics get some fresh goodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T22:47:20-07:00","id":180455,"title":"","content":"Stigmatics got some neat merits, including a Super Friend Demon merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T22:57:47-07:00","id":180461,"title":"","content":"So far I'm loving it, so many possibilities. Demonic form powers &quot;Collapsible&quot; and &quot;Shielded Compartment&quot; + &quot;bolthole-easy access&quot; + overly trusting demons = Russian Nesting Demons. Have the head demon with the demon form power &quot;Shielded Compartment&quot; and the merit &quot;Bolthole - Easy Access&quot; spend a point of aether to turn his little door into his bolt hole, get heaps of demons with the Collapsible demon form power to shrink down and cram in the bolt hole. It'd be a super convenient way to get a whole army of demons into a place where they could really f@%&amp; stuff up with a surprise attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T00:28:22-07:00","id":180491,"title":"","content":"My very first impression: It has a Table of Contents! Not that one-page thing listing chapter headings and their page numbers that White Wolf traditionally passed off as a Table of Contents, but an actual, in-depth outline of what\u2019s in the book and where it can be found!<br /> <br /> Now if only the preview were one page longer \u2014 or four, so as to include the first two pages of the Introduction (including the \u201cWhat\u2019s In This Book?\u201d section)\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T00:30:33-07:00","id":180494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180491#post180491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My very first impression: It has a Table of Contents! Not that one-page thing listing chapter headings and their page numbers that White Wolf traditionally passed off as a Table of Contents, but an actual, in-depth outline of what\u2019s in the book and where it can be found!<br /> <br /> Now if only the preview were one page longer \u2014 or four, so as to include the first two pages of the Introduction (including the \u201cWhat\u2019s In This Book?\u201d section)\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I noticed as well but it's more of an issue with Drivethru than OP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T00:57:01-07:00","id":180501,"title":"","content":"The Sanctity of Merits and Covers sidebar reminded me of a house rule I use: where it makes sense to do so, I allow players to assign individual Merits to specific Covers. The downside is that the Merit is only available when in that Cover; the upside is that you can use to Sanctity of Merits rule to \u201credistribute\u201d your Cover-specific Merit dots in other Covers (for this purpose, the Demonic Form counts as a Cover). So the businessman has plenty of Resources, while the math teacher has Contacts at the local university.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T02:25:56-07:00","id":180547,"title":"","content":"Any info on new Agendas? I'm hoping something more &quot;demonic&quot; or &quot;angelic&quot; to see.<br /> <br /> Also, is there a way to &quot;steal&quot; a body of Cover, much more like Possesion, than creation of new being? Think <i>Supernatural </i>(TV show<i>) </i>demons and angles Vessels possessions. Is there anything like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-26-2014, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T05:41:26-07:00","id":180718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180547#post180547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any info on new Agendas? I'm hoping something more &quot;demonic&quot; or &quot;angelic&quot; to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core four get more information, and there's a little more information on Descent philosophies based on Agendas, which I found very useful.<br /> No new Agendas as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180547#post180547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is there a way to &quot;steal&quot; a body of Cover, much more like Possesion, than creation of new being? Think <i>Supernatural </i>(TV show<i>) </i>demons and angles Vessels possessions. Is there anything like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>What little there was on the subject concentrated mostly on maintaining multiple Covers.<br /> <br /> Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T06:04:21-07:00","id":180730,"title":"","content":"Sad Hamster, nothing interesting for him... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T06:48:27-07:00","id":180754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180227#post180227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can say is damn... Lamba Gadgets are insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moo hoo ha ha ha!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T07:10:32-07:00","id":180767,"title":"","content":"Impressions:<br /> <br /> Front cover is sexy as hell, pun intended. First piece of demon art I actually enjoyed.<br /> <br /> Opening fiction is likewise awesome. Thoroughly enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> After that, we get into the meat of the book. I feel like there's actually two parts to this book, all in all. <br /> <br /> The first is a series of essays on how to see things like your Cover, Rings, Agendas or Agencies; also, a bit on Infrastructure. There's a few new rules on how to handle things like faking emotions. But, overall, I feel like this section is just a major disappointment. For the most part, it just reiterates the same material from the core book. If you had trouble grasping the idea of the Unchained as Fallen Angels or had trouble wrapping your head around some other part of the game, then this section is for you. If you had a strong grasp of the core game already, then you're just wading through so many words. I feel like this part of the book is more set on pushing stereotypes than broadening different avenues of play. <br /> <br /> <br /> One exception - there's a section on suborning Infrastructure, which is handy. It gives a couple new ways to analyze and get into how demons interact with Infrastructure. It has new rules for how to analyze and adapt to such places, and taking its power for your own. I appreciated it far more than any of the other parts, though it may be because I didn't entirely grasp that part of the core book myself - someone else may find that section to be dull as I find the Agencies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Second half of the book is crammed full of new mechanics to play with. New Embeds, new Exploits, new Demon Forms, new ways to use and abuse gadgets. And, yes, Lambda are sexy as sin; something tells me that a lot of players are going to be jumping at the chance to make them. My only complaint is that it feels like boltholes are becoming less compelling as the demon's Safe Place merit, as you can't actually make your hole into a protected workshop. So, sorry, but no hidden hell-forge for you to keep tucked away in a hidden dimension.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T07:43:59-07:00","id":180802,"title":"","content":"That's good to hear. Whenever I've seen someone express that they have a hard time understanding Infrastructure and how to hack it, I've been thinking &quot;Well, I explain it in detail in the Player's Guide&quot;. Treating the God-Machine's occult matrices as a computer script, and what you can do to twist it to your own advantage.<br /> <br /> I suspect you're right, in that different readers will appreciate different parts of the first two chapters depending on what they had a hard time understanding. That's what players' guides are <i>for</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T09:20:52-07:00","id":180843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180767#post180767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaint is that it feels like boltholes are becoming less compelling as the demon's Safe Place merit, as you can't actually make your hole into a protected workshop. So, sorry, but no hidden hell-forge for you to keep tucked away in a hidden dimension.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I bet that requirement could be waived if you took the merit that lets you start out with subverted infrastructure that gives off Aether. I think that one's in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T09:31:51-07:00","id":180909,"title":"","content":"So, Exploited gadgets can't retain their original function? Does this mean you can't make a crazy looking sci-fi car that has been exploited with Rip the Gates? Maybe instead, it would make more sense to say...exploit your car's radio into a flux capacitor, so to speak?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T10:56:58-07:00","id":180993,"title":"","content":"Some of Chapter 1 was redundant for me, but I liked seeing it written out the way it was anyway because it helped me think it through better. Also, it gave me some other considerations on things like memory and the demonic form.<br /> <br /> The chapter on Infrastructure and Agencies is worth its weight in gold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:07:30-07:00","id":181011,"title":"","content":"So, I'm in Chapter 2 as far as proper reading, and a question occurs to me: could a demon learn enough about infrastructure and occult matrices that, with enough suborning, hacking,and other work(ie, making this at least the process of a story, if not an arc or chronicle),could a demon summon an angel?<br /> <br /> I mean, in a certain way, some Embeds and Exploits already poke at creating self-aware appendages that enact the Demon's will-Alibi and Terrible Avatar are the first to come to mind, but there's a few more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:29:59-07:00","id":181049,"title":"","content":"To whoever wrote the section on Gadgets,<br /> <br /> Bravo. Truly, that was everything I could have hoped for and more. Reading through it I felt a little smile of pride creep onto my face, seeing so much excellence come out of something that received so little space in the core book.<br /> <br /> Again, bravo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:39:40-07:00","id":181072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=181011#post181011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm in Chapter 2 as far as proper reading, and a question occurs to me: could a demon learn enough about infrastructure and occult matrices that, with enough suborning, hacking,and other work(ie, making this at least the process of a story, if not an arc or chronicle),could a demon summon an angel?<br /> <br /> I mean, in a certain way, some Embeds and Exploits already poke at creating self-aware appendages that enact the Demon's will-Alibi and Terrible Avatar are the first to come to mind, but there's a few more.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they correctly ascertain that a Project is designed to summon an angel, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:42:25-07:00","id":181078,"title":"","content":"A minor grump, but given it sounds like a player aspiration can be (particularly for Integrators) to become an Exile, I was kind of hoping we'd get some Exile mechanics here. Little sad that didn't pan out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:46:34-07:00","id":181086,"title":"","content":"I figured more on Exiles would show up in the Storyteller's Guide, since even if you can play it should be something you learn through the course of the chronicle, and therefore not really general player based stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:51:06-07:00","id":181090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=181072#post181072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they correctly ascertain that a Project is designed to summon an angel, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And with that, Wednesday is going to enslave the world (or at least Seattle) to take out the God-Machine. Thanks, I got what I needed, the rest of this book is just delicious, joyful filler.<br /> <br /> Seriously, you could have released Chapter 2 by itself and I'd be pleased as punch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T12:23:29-07:00","id":181156,"title":"","content":"One thing that's really fun about this book is its willingness to embrace crossover and even devote wordcount to powers that specifically deal with other gamelines and their supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Every time a supplement does that, the world of darkness seems a little bit bigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T12:55:56-07:00","id":181176,"title":"","content":"The book has been bought... now have to wait through today to download it to my computer... today is going to be a long day. I want to read it so bad! I want to know what these Lambda Gadgets people are talking about are!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:57:16-07:00","id":181273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=181176#post181176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book has been bought... now have to wait through today to download it to my computer... today is going to be a long day. I want to read it so bad! I want to know what these Lambda Gadgets people are talking about are!</div> </div> </div> </div>In effect, what happens when you weld one Gadget to another Gadget, fusing the embedded Embeds/Exploits.<br /> <br /> It's also possible to fuse a Lambda to a <i>third </i>Gadget, but given how unless you're really skilled <i>and </i>really lucky, what you'll likely make instead is an Aetheric mushroom cloud that powers a neon sign screaming INSANE DEMON HERE in Angelese, those things are MacGuffins (the guide calls out only five as known to still exist).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T15:08:24-07:00","id":181281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180547#post180547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is there a way to &quot;steal&quot; a body of Cover, much more like Possesion, than creation of new being? Think <i>Supernatural </i>(TV show<i>) </i>demons and angles Vessels possessions. Is there anything like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welll...there's one merit that, while it doesn't serve your immediate needs, can be used as a seed for what you want. The Sleeve Integrator Merit allows a Stigmatic possessing it to spend a WP to open himself up to merging with an Unchained for a day in exchange for learning some Embeds, acting as a new Cover in every way. In your games, what you could do is follow suit and allow some Stigmatics (or maybe all of them - it's your show!) to exist as another source of long-term covers as long as the Unchained can gain consent. Doing so will add another dimension to a war over Stigmatic allies, and it'll add some measure of the Vessels to your game at the cost of deemphasizing pacts a little.<br /> <br /> You could even allow angels to do the same thing, although I probably wouldn't even if I was going for a more Supernatural twist on it. Do what thou wilt, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 06-26-2014, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T15:10:12-07:00","id":181283,"title":"","content":"They do give an example of a Second Order Lambda, the Dreaming Machine.<br /> <br /> It's pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T15:12:59-07:00","id":181285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=181273#post181273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In effect, what happens when you weld one Gadget to another Gadget, fusing the embedded Embeds/Exploits.<br /> <br /> It's also possible to fuse a Lambda to a <i>third </i>Gadget, but given how unless you're really skilled <i>and </i>really lucky, what you'll likely make instead is an Aetheric mushroom cloud that powers a neon sign screaming INSANE DEMON HERE in Angelese, those things are MacGuffins (the guide calls out only five as known to still exist).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's half the fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T16:08:15-07:00","id":181333,"title":"","content":"A no-prize to the first person who can work out why I called them lambdas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T16:46:52-07:00","id":181394,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a programming term involving the combination of two functions into one. See <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lambda_calculus\" target=\"_blank\">Lambda Calculus</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T17:51:43-07:00","id":181477,"title":"","content":"Question. Do you always have to take the willpower dot hit for <i>all </i>Gadgets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T18:30:28-07:00","id":181496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=181394#post181394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a programming term involving the combination of two functions into one. See <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lambda_calculus\" target=\"_blank\">Lambda Calculus</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum.. I mostly know it from my Python course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T18:56:16-07:00","id":181507,"title":"","content":"I am hyped.<br /> <br /> Waiting for my lunchbreak so I can sit and read this at Uni between writing pages and pages of words!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T19:28:15-07:00","id":181545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=180271#post180271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apple of Discord. TO be fair the myth came before My Little Pony did it, but I can't think of someone <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fX5nDlafVEc\" target=\"_blank\">doing a song</a> to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hilariously close to the mark. I never thought I'd be doing research on My Little Pony episodes, but here we are.<br /> <br /> The first seed of the idea for me came from Pulp Fiction, actually. We see the trope in The Maltese Falcon, and I was tempted to say something about MacGuffins but figured the developer would probably shoot that name down. So I went with the classic tale.<br /> <br /> The &quot;or person&quot; language is there because I remembered There's Something About Mary and Helen of Troy, the latter of whom is closely connected to the Apple of Discord story anyway (she was Paris's reward for declaring Venus the fairest of the goddesses, and that sparked a war).<br /> <br /> It's definitely one of those powers I would find a bunch of devious and arguably morally reprehensible uses for if I were playing in a Demon game. Things like dropping a quarter in a crowded public space and making my escape in the confusion. I hope others get good use out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 06-27-2014, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T23:58:38-07:00","id":181728,"title":"","content":"Okay, I really liked the book, but I couldn't wait til I was actually fully awake to read it, so perhaps a few things flew by my sleepy head, that being said.....<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing a lot of point in embed tattoo gadgets. Other than imprinting near field powers to expand the demon's bag of tricks, unless one allows one to change the dice pool, but that's when the medium of the gadget causes the dice pool to change, is inking them on a demon warrant allowing the demon changing the dice pool? Because honestly that's not something I'd allow if I were running a demon game unless the book specifically says &quot;Yes, the demon can change the dice pool by inking their embed.&quot;<br /> <br /> The urban legend power seems a little weird to me, making urban legends sorta true so that demons can use them for facades. But urban legends are already true, there are alligators in the sewers, Bloody Mary collects little kid faces, and the Jersey Devil flies to this day (I used to want to add him to a hunter campaign, have him be the missing lucifuge member, but now with heirs to hell I could see him the result of a demon daddy going loud while the mrs was pregnant). So the premise of making something real more real just seems pretty darn odd to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T06:31:21-07:00","id":181854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=181728#post181728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Okay, I really liked the book, but I couldn't wait til I was actually fully awake to read it, so perhaps a few things flew by my sleepy head, that being said.....<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing a lot of point in embed tattoo gadgets. Other than imprinting near field powers to expand the demon's bag of tricks, unless one allows one to change the dice pool, but that's when the medium of the gadget causes the dice pool to change, is inking them on a demon warrant allowing the demon changing the dice pool? Because honestly that's not something I'd allow if I were running a demon game unless the book specifically says &quot;Yes, the demon can change the dice pool by inking their embed.&quot;<br /> <br /> The urban legend power seems a little weird to me, making urban legends sorta true so that demons can use them for facades. But urban legends are already true, there are alligators in the sewers, Bloody Mary collects little kid faces, and the Jersey Devil flies to this day (I used to want to add him to a hunter campaign, have him be the missing lucifuge member, but now with heirs to hell I could see him the result of a demon daddy going loud while the mrs was pregnant). So the premise of making something real more real just seems pretty darn odd to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some Urban Legends aren't real! And then you make them real.<br /> <br /> On a different note, I'm a little torn. It feels like a waste of Willpower dots (and thus, XP) to have to burn it to make a batch of One-Offs. Is it really intended that you need to, or they actually cost-effective?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 06-27-2014, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T07:07:18-07:00","id":181908,"title":"","content":"In regards Urban Legend in to the World of Darkness, the thing about it being a mystery setting is that not every urban legend can be true. Sometimes, things are just stories. Even worse, sometimes bad things happen without any supernatural help.<br /> <br /> But it makes a damn good Cover if it were.Hence,Urban Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:07:00-07:00","id":182023,"title":"","content":"Actually, thanks to Changeling, even untrue urban legends are true, seeing as how there are keeper versions of Bloody Mary and the Hook. <br /> <br /> So actually this is a trick done a lot more effectively in changeling.<br /> <br /> And what is so special about urban legends? Tapping into the power of people's belief in something true? In nwod, you can say the same for everything from lovecraftian horror to fairy tales. <br /> <br /> Are urban legends examples of wild occult <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">matrices? If so wouldn't using this power be a big neon sign to the god-machine reading &quot;pay attention to me?&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:09:55-07:00","id":182025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=181908#post181908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards Urban Legend in to the World of Darkness, the thing about it being a mystery setting is that not every urban legend can be true. Sometimes, things are just stories. Even worse, sometimes bad things happen without any supernatural help.<br /> But it makes a damn good Cover if it were.Hence,Urban Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, unless I'm misreading something (this is one of David Hill's, so I have no authorial insight on this one), the demon can spin an urban legend out of whole cloth, have it infect the human rumor mill, and make herself a part of it. Ask the bartenders around town about that mad cult leader you're &quot;investigating,&quot; and you can step in the role of one of his imaginary cultists. Create a Tumblr documenting the crimes of the gang that's been roughing up old ladies, and become one of the gang members or one of their victims. Tell a story about the masked hero who watches over Seattle and become his sidekick or a member of his rogues gallery (an extreme and admittedly silly example and one that won't give you superpowers, but you get the idea).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:24:06-07:00","id":182042,"title":"","content":"1)True, but Demon does still largely play to it's own context, since whether or not Changelings exist is a ST fiat. So keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> 2)What happens in Arcadia doesn't provide context for what happens in the world.<br /> <br /> 3)Changelings can't generate 'people'(well, video game NPC's really) to go enact a story, they can make people who live close to patterns become utterly ensnared in them. In a certain sense, the demon can do it with less blood, or at least less risk to actual people. But it depends on the effect you want.<br /> <br /> 4)You are creating temporary people to enact a narrative for whatever reason best works for you, and you can hop into one of these bit roles to go and do whatever shit you want/can as that role. THere's a lot you can do with Urban Legend.<br /> <br /> 5)There's a relationship here that I think you might be missing. A lot of the things in the WoD aren't true because people believe in them, people 'believe' in them because they are true.<br /> <br /> People also believe a lot of false things. Frightful memes mutate and become something wholly new. Demons can take advantage of that faster that most. (And to be fair[as an example], Slenderman is totally their sort of game, a dark fairytale fueled by modern fears and backed by quantum myth)<br /> <br /> 6)It's like a occult matrix given form by the masses and life by the Demon.<br /> <br /> 7)It's an Exploit. All of them are big neon signs reading &quot;PAY ATTENTION TO ME!&quot;<br /> <br /> 8)EDIT: Consider some of the fiction for WoD, particularly <i>Strangeness in the Proportion</i>, where all things are true, but there's still a pervasiveness of folklore, myth, and urban legends that aren't true. Simon said that out of the thousands of autopsies he performed, none really seemed the result of supernatural involvement.<br /> <br /> Yes, the World of Darkness is filled to the gills with supernatural baddies, but quite frankly it's still so big that not everything is absolutely covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-27-2014, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T11:19:56-07:00","id":182115,"title":"","content":"Finally hit payday! The book is downloading now. In the meantime, I bet the new Perturbator album resonates with more than a few of the Unchained...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://fbcdn-sphotos-b-a.akamaihd.net/hphotos-ak-xap1/t1.0-9/p403x403/10274300_810626048969561_6677526698933053481_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T13:09:14-07:00","id":182177,"title":"","content":"So I was wondering, aside from not being able to use powers that require extended actions, what are the limitations to Show of Power? Could a werewolf's shape shifting ability be used since it only requires a reflexive action? What about Disciplines, Gifts, Rotes, etc? If something like Garau form was available, how would one determine how long it lasts, or would it last the entire scene since it is an inherent ability? Would they be subject to Death Rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T14:30:24-07:00","id":182233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badger King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182177#post182177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was wondering, aside from not being able to use powers that require extended actions, what are the limitations to Show of Power? Could a werewolf's shape shifting ability be used since it only requires a reflexive action? What about Disciplines, Gifts, Rotes, etc? If something like Garau form was available, how would one determine how long it lasts, or would it last the entire scene since it is an inherent ability? Would they be subject to Death Rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair questions all. There would have been literally no way to address all of them in the write-up of a single Exploit, so I'm afraid there will necessarily be some group discussion and ST discretion involved. RAW gives you a lot of leeway, and I'm not going to say &quot;this is the right way to interpret the power and this other way is bad-wrong fun and forbidden.&quot; Enough with my standard caveats, though.<br /> <br /> That said, I originally conceived of Show of Power as primarily a &quot;convince them that I'm one of them&quot; power with a side of &quot;convince them that I'm something supernatural but not a demon.&quot; I wrote it immediately after Deep Cover, which serves a similar purpose to a lesser degree. In essence, the intention is for the demon to be able to pretend to be a mage or werewolf or vampire or whatever without being immediately detected because he can't cast spells/shift/use Disciplines/whatever. But it's supposed to be juuuust enough to fake it, not enough to be impressive at it. Thus the exclusion of extended actions, the limit of one success, and the minimal number of factors. When someone says, &quot;You're no mage! You're a demon!&quot; you can &quot;prove&quot; you're a mage using, well, a small show of power.<br /> <br /> From that perspective, I'd say werewolf form? Yes because how can you pretend to be a werewolf if you can't change shapes? Rotes? Kind of. I mean sure, wiggle your fingers all you want and mumble convincing arcane babble, but it isn't going to give you a bonus to your make-magic-go roll so it's just Rote theater. Burning in the sun? Usually optional, but sometimes the only way to convince the Anarchs that you're not a spy is to spend some Aether so you can get a nasty sunburn when the situation calls for it. Gotta keep up appearances if you want to stay alive in this biz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T15:16:51-07:00","id":182255,"title":"","content":"Using this little trick to burn in the sun; I love that idea. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T15:33:45-07:00","id":182284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182233#post182233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair questions all. There would have been literally no way to address all of them in the write-up of a single Exploit, so I'm afraid there will necessarily be some group discussion and ST discretion involved. RAW gives you a lot of leeway, and I'm not going to say &quot;this is the right way to interpret the power and this other way is bad-wrong fun and forbidden.&quot; Enough with my standard caveats, though.<br /> <br /> That said, I originally conceived of Show of Power as primarily a &quot;convince them that I'm one of them&quot; power with a side of &quot;convince them that I'm something supernatural but not a demon.&quot; I wrote it immediately after Deep Cover, which serves a similar purpose to a lesser degree. In essence, the intention is for the demon to be able to pretend to be a mage or werewolf or vampire or whatever without being immediately detected because he can't cast spells/shift/use Disciplines/whatever. But it's supposed to be juuuust enough to fake it, not enough to be impressive at it. Thus the exclusion of extended actions, the limit of one success, and the minimal number of factors. When someone says, &quot;You're no mage! You're a demon!&quot; you can &quot;prove&quot; you're a mage using, well, a small show of power.<br /> <br /> From that perspective, I'd say werewolf form? Yes because how can you pretend to be a werewolf if you can't change shapes? Rotes? Kind of. I mean sure, wiggle your fingers all you want and mumble convincing arcane babble, but it isn't going to give you a bonus to your make-magic-go roll so it's just Rote theater. Burning in the sun? Usually optional, but sometimes the only way to convince the Anarchs that you're not a spy is to spend some Aether so you can get a nasty sunburn when the situation calls for it. Gotta keep up appearances if you want to stay alive in this biz.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that. I thought of something else that I figure might come up since I plan on starting up a game of DtD soon, and I figure certain people in the group would want to try and push that power to the limit.Say someone wanted to mimic a power like Celerity; would they only be able to mimic the part of the powers that are Reflexive actions like interrupting anothers action or getting to the top of the initiative, or would they also be able to mimic the persistent effect? If the persistent power can be mimicked, how would one determine how many ranks it would have?<br /> <br /> I like the power and see where you intended for it to be a way to blend in, but I see some players trying to use it to make themselves more combat efficient and kind of want a starting point to determine how generous I should be. I figure, more than a single rank in something like Celerity would be good, but if you don't mind, your input as the designer would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:00:33-07:00","id":182313,"title":"","content":"A thing that came up while talking with a friend: What sort of effects can Show of Power produce when Installed into a gadget?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:14:59-07:00","id":182344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182313#post182313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing that came up while talking with a friend: What sort of effects can Show of Power produce when Installed into a gadget?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps a wand that allows you to unveil a Nimbus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:40:45-07:00","id":182365,"title":"","content":"Finally finished the book last night. There's a power called Demon Car that allows you to merge with your car into a demon car. This automatically makes this the best book ever*.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Okay, so I think it's actually pretty decent. I agree with an above poster that the first chapter's pretty much just a rehash of information you already knew from the core or could extrapolate from there, aside from a few parts. Decently written, probably useful for those that need it spelled out, but I didn't see as much interesting or innovative stuff in the text as I was personally hoping for. From then on the book gets better and better: chapter two is pretty useful, chapter three is the toybox full of neat new toys (like Demon Car(!)), and chapter 4 is a bunch of sorely needed and incredibly interesting expansion and twists on gadgets.<br /> <br /> All in all, well worth the money. I'll be picking it up in PoD as soon as it launches.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Seriously, though, Demon Car rules. The only issue I have is that you could have called it &quot;Hell On Wheels&quot; but you didn't. Come oooooon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:56:15-07:00","id":182376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badger King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182284#post182284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for that. I thought of something else that I figure might come up since I plan on starting up a game of DtD soon, and I figure certain people in the group would want to try and push that power to the limit.Say someone wanted to mimic a power like Celerity; would they only be able to mimic the part of the powers that are Reflexive actions like interrupting anothers action or getting to the top of the initiative, or would they also be able to mimic the persistent effect? If the persistent power can be mimicked, how would one determine how many ranks it would have?<br /> <br /> I like the power and see where you intended for it to be a way to blend in, but I see some players trying to use it to make themselves more combat efficient and kind of want a starting point to determine how generous I should be. I figure, more than a single rank in something like Celerity would be good, but if you don't mind, your input as the designer would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize this is of finite use to a ST looking for guidance, but this is definitely one of those powers that you really have to adjudicate as you go. That said, here are a couple words of comfort? Warning? Something like that.<br /> <br /> First, I will point out that each power the demon &quot;fakes&quot; requires a separate use of this Exploit, and every use of it costs Aether and constitutes a compromise. Nor does access to a particular ability last forever. Even if you spend a year masquerading as splats X, Y, Z, and Q, learning their kung fu, er, powers so you can be the biggest badass ever, simply &quot;powering up&quot; all those kewl muuvs has a good chance of bringing a choir of hunter angels down on your head. Demons already have the option of Going Loud, and a dozen compromises in a single scene sounds to me like just a slower way to do that.<br /> <br /> Another balancing aspect is the demon can't mimic a power he hasn't experienced or encountered first-hand. As ST that means that you have a pretty decent amount of control over what powers that demon acquires via Show of Power. Don't want him to pick up ridiculous amounts of Celerity? Don't bring in vampires with tons of Celerity into the game. Yes, he's going to learn every power you use against him and turn it against the next batch of baddies you bring out, but the ST has considerable control over the speed with which that cold war progresses.<br /> <br /> I totally understand how clever players could find ways to abuse this Exploit, but I also see ways that clever players can be, well, clever with it. I can imagine a demon who has spent a decade or more apprenticed to a mage, carefully pretending to be one of the Wise herself, and has access to a fairly huge range of spells as a result, and I can see the concept as either a horribly twinked out Sam Haight Special (in the worst cWoD sense) or a really nifty character with a complex Cover to maintain (especially as a bizarre antagonist). It's up to the player (and the ST) to determine whether the execution of that concept is awesome or just dumb.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps you somewhat, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T17:03:44-07:00","id":182378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182313#post182313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing that came up while talking with a friend: What sort of effects can Show of Power produce when Installed into a gadget?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're terrible people!<br /> <br /> ...with a really nifty idea.<br /> <br /> Hm. I'd probably limit it to one specific power per Gadget for stuff that requires activation, or maybe a small grab bag of inherent or basic template powers, but I'm sure there are other ways to do it. Suddenly you end up with Exploited Gadgets that act like the relics/artifacts/etc. of other splats. There have to be stories in that. I mean *besides* Needful Things the Consilium Edition. *smirk*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T17:14:17-07:00","id":182384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby