the best thing <i>ever</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The note that it works on <i>any vehicle</i> below the Size limit is especially welcome to my nautical Guardian with designs on flotilla-ing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">oh god demonic penny-farthing</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T19:50:05-07:00","id":182446,"title":"","content":"Picked FoH up today, and I love it - especially the details on suborning Infrastructure for more than just an Aether source (my Tempter is definitely going to have fun with that).<br /> <br /> I'm left with a couple of questions, though:<br /> <br /> First, Laser Cutter. Acidic Spit (also a Technology) does damage based on successes and at greater range, and the damage is Aggravated, bypassing mundane Durability entirely (unless that got changed somewhere and I missed it). I'm guessing, given that it isn't stated, that Laser Cutter's damage is Lethal. Does Laser Cutter bypass the set amount of Durability on magic objects? Does it add its damage to successes, or just inflict the stated amount regardless of successes? (My guess is that it adds to successes, given that the Dex + Crafts roll when using it to break an immobile, unattended object wouldn't make much sense otherwise, but I didn't see anything to support this in the way the form's rules are worded.) Is it even possible for Laser Cutter to penetrate, for example, the Durability 10 bank vault in the base blue book? Is it just strictly worse than Acidic Spit, or am I getting confused somewhere?<br /> <br /> Second: Would it be unreasonable to conclude that, to free the hand if necessary, a Demon can reflexively engage and disengage Eliminator Cannon as with Blade Hand or Rivet Arm? The Demon would still have to let go of anything held in hand to engage the weapon, as with the other two. I'm asking this one because both of the latter mention under Appearance that the form replaces a hand like Eliminator Cannon (though DtD mentions that the forms' appearances can be changed within reason to fit the Demon anyway), but also mention the reflexive &quot;draw/stow&quot; under system, while Eliminator Cannon says nothing in either direction under system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3388,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","user":"r0gue_rob0t","date":". 06-27-2014, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","name":"r0gue_rob0t","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:40:14-07:00","id":182584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182413#post182413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AW, I should have thought of Hell on Wheels.<br /> <br /> By the way, yes, Demon car is the best thing <i>ever</i>.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy theory about a conspiracy: the Client for the Knights of Saint Adrian is not an angel or even the God-Machine, but an Integrator with Tattoo Gadgets and a crazy plan to get back.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well you'd have to houserule that one can make tattoo gadgets on anyone other than themselves, but that was kind of a weird limitation anyway. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:50:10-07:00","id":182596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182378#post182378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're terrible people!<br /> <br /> ...with a really nifty idea.<br /> <br /> Hm. I'd probably limit it to one specific power per Gadget for stuff that requires activation, or maybe a small grab bag of inherent or basic template powers, but I'm sure there are other ways to do it. Suddenly you end up with Exploited Gadgets that act like the relics/artifacts/etc. of other splats. There have to be stories in that. I mean *besides* Needful Things the Consilium Edition. *smirk*</div> </div> </div> </div> I imagine that exploit would be especially fun when incorporated into a lambda gadget. <br /> <br /> Like say combined with the 'make a ghost or spirit cover&quot; perhaps it would allow one to take on powers as part of their cover, or combine it with the urban legend power and become a monster.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:51:50-07:00","id":182598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182584#post182584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you'd have to houserule that one can make tattoo gadgets on anyone other than themselves, but that was kind of a weird limitation anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to Hunter! You must be new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:44:26-07:00","id":183054,"title":"","content":"So, let's say someone uses Going Native and then someone uses Wave Function Collapse on that first person. Are they stuck as humans for hours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:45:53-07:00","id":183056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182378#post182378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're terrible people!<br /> <br /> ...with a really nifty idea.<br /> <br /> Hm. I'd probably limit it to one specific power per Gadget for stuff that requires activation, or maybe a small grab bag of inherent or basic template powers, but I'm sure there are other ways to do it. Suddenly you end up with Exploited Gadgets that act like the relics/artifacts/etc. of other splats. There have to be stories in that. I mean *besides* Needful Things the Consilium Edition. *smirk*</div> </div> </div> </div>A set of plastic vampire teeth that, when activated, give you a grab bag of vampire abilities.<br /> <br /> Better yet, a black cape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T20:27:04-07:00","id":183452,"title":"","content":"Impressions: Really liked this one, and I think is going to be essential material for running a DtD game, as there is going to be a lot of things that will come up in games.<ul><li>I'm very glad the developers took the word count to add more inspirational material. The original book was a little scant, considering that DtD is kinda off the walls, more inspiration is always good.</li> <li>I'm... not thrilled that they added more dice mechanics to the cover mechanics, one of the strengths of the story-teller system was minimizing dice rolling, but there are some nice story hooks here, such as keeping an abusive ex-spouse alive so he can continue to support your cover. Or Visiting the funeral of a friend to make sure the people there remember you enough to maintain your cover. Gives demons more an incentive to hang around humans.</li> <li>Agendas. Nice, but I wish there was more material difference between</li> <li>Incarnations. Say thoughts as Agendas</li> <li>Infrastructure. If there are any developers reading I have only one thing to say: I WANT MORE.</li> <li>Agencies. I always had trouble understanding why a demon would expose themselves to the risk of joining an agency, with so few up front benefits. The answer: <i>ambition</i>, agencies are what happens when a demon decides &quot;go pro or go home.&quot;</li> <li>New Embeds and Exploits: Mixed. Some are brilliant, some are a little too situational to be useful (Fractal Reality jumps to mind)</li> <li>Gadgets: New options, more in-story justification</li> </ul><br /> What I would have wanted (because I'm greedy):<ul><li>Options for playing exiles</li> <li>Options for playing Cryptids</li> <li>Angel Gadgets. You heard me. Get an angel, by hook, crook, or bargain to put a numen in a gadget.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T20:59:08-07:00","id":183470,"title":"","content":"Finally finished with the book! Overall, I'd say it's solid; not amazing, not bad, not even mediocre, but just effective. The redundancy in Chapter 1 was welcome for me, you can't go wrong with new powers to play with, and I don't think it did anything <i>wrong</i>, but it was lacking a few things I was hoping for.<ul><li>Sympathetic Integrators: they're my favorite Agenda, and <i>Flowers</i> doesn't do enough to make them feel like a character choice most would want to make.</li> <li>Hell: tragically little discussion on Hell, considering how major a goal it is to some. I wanted examples of what physical Hell would look like.</li> <li>Agencies: what's there is fine, but I wanted a few example groups! The group that Comrade West runs in Seattle is fascinating, but I had my fingers crossed for examples of Agencies at each of the Tiers, with variable memberships and goals. The guidelines we got felt a little &quot;duh!&quot; to me.</li> <li>Demonic Form abilities: my least-favorite bit of Demon character creation, and the options here still felt unexciting to me. Maybe I'm impossible to please.</li> <li>Exiles: the cousins of the Unchained probably belong in the Storyteller book, but I'm so damn eager to find out more about them!</li> <li>Cryptid Familiars: I think everyone wants these.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T21:06:53-07:00","id":183472,"title":"","content":"So I finished Flowers of Hell. On the whole, I'm wildly pleased with the product-it was a legitimate joy to read. I felt like it answered some of my smaller wants, from Going Native answer my idle thought of comparison to Doctor Who to the Gadget chapter placing time limits and stake on mortal usage, which has been the center conflict of a story brewing in my head for a long while now.<br /> <br /> The first chapter neatly expanded demon capability and philosophy and really did give me a great sense of what it was like to live as a demon, both the good, the bad, and above all else the tenseness of that life.<br /> <br /> I have sung praises about the second chapter and will do so again: this sort of thing was the first question I had for Demon The Descent upon finishing the first chapter, and it was delivered quite reasonably-it's big, but not world breaking, risky to do, and story generating. THe discussions on Infrastructure doubled down on this, and the bonus of Agenda creation, while perhaps a little tedious, was an extended bonus.<br /> <br /> Chapter Three was a glorious grab bag, and like I said, a lot of little desires were hit. Some additional ones were Newton's Nightmares, which felt like a great reinterpretation and execution of the Lore of the Fundament from <i>Fallen, </i>Show of Power and Deep Cover for mimicking supernaturals(a great interest of mine since the beginning), Walls of Jericho and Stop for just being brutal, Demon Car and Terrible Avatar for exapnding the Demonic form's usage(and again to Terrible Avatar for hitting a major itch for my favorite demon), Ripple, Trip, Fractal Reality, and Victory at Any Price for perpetuating the momentum of any action scene, particularly combat, Apple of Discord(Want It Need It Spell) simply for making me smile, High of Birth for it's great player-made plot hooks, Knock-off just for being awesome, Open Sesame and Wasted Time for making sneaking in more fun and easy, the <i>entire Mundane list for being awesome as Hell</i>, Imagine for making John Lennon scary and exciting again, The Look for taking me back to younger days(Ruroni Kenshin, not some dark thing), Loose Lips and The Only Word That Matters for making dialogue a knife edge, Detachable Limbs for taking me back to my youth(Power Rangers, not some dark thing), Laser Cutter for having a hydro version that makes me want to read Battle Angel Alita again, Low-I'm just listing the whole damn chapter. Point is there was always something fun in the bag.<br /> <br /> Chapter Four was the hardest one to read for me, but considering I have a story I want to write around this it was all useful, and I'm considering what else I can do with the other things like Form Gadgets and Lambdas for that. The new gadgets are all awesome, and I want to make a Lambda built on Incendiary an Combustion(and maybe another, if I'm cheeky?) that has the activation code &quot;Kieru!&quot; or &quot;Disappear!&quot;. Fire that on Overcharge. Speaking of, the sample Newton's Nightmares Gadget almost matches a weapon I gave a TF:V agent a few years ago that he claimed was from Roswell, except that also fractured space around the target point so you couldn't really leave within a certain point. I wonder if that was one of the five second-order Lambdas now. Form Gadgets are an excellent way to expand demonic forms even further, knockoffs and one shots are appreciated-just lots of good stuff.<br /> <br /> I suppose my only complaint with this is something I never wanted to say, given how many people griped about it and I thought it was silly: the language really is moving away from the sense of the divine rebels. It's less Rakshasas and Daevas and Asuras in this book, and definitely more arcane physics/spy thriller stuff. That's hardly a deal breaker for me, and I can always inject more on my own, but it finally did grain against me.<br /> <br /> That's a small price to pay, though. All of this book is awesome, Chapters One and Two in particular. It expands stories I had, gives me new ones to tell, and spirals off into places between. Good job guys-you've definitely secured Demon as my second favorite RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T21:40:32-07:00","id":183505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=183472#post183472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose my only complaint with this is something I never wanted to say, given how many people griped about it and I thought it was silly: the language really is moving away from the sense of the divine rebels.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, &quot;pulled into the orbit of Fallen angels&quot; remains one of my favorite little phrases from the book, and the vast majority of the example sobriquets for the angels who acted as the starting point for ways the Unchained take their catalysts were decidedly more poetic than I would have expected.<br /> <br /> Besides which, <i>Steins;Gate</i> is a thriller, and that's a story I'm fond of describing as the leadup to a modern prophet's attempt to thwart God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:09:05-07:00","id":183800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=183505#post183505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, &quot;pulled into the orbit of Fallen angels&quot; remains one of my favorite little phrases from the book, and the vast majority of the example sobriquets for the angels who acted as the starting point for ways the Unchained take their catalysts were decidedly more poetic than I would have expected.<br /> <br /> Besides which, <i>Steins;Gate</i> is a thriller, and that's a story I'm fond of describing as the leadup to a modern prophet's attempt to thwart God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I loved the artistry of that phrase too! Also, yes, someone was having fun with the Catalyst section.<br /> <br /> One of the things I love about Demon is that it's linguistic synergy is really top notch-the divine meets the tech meets the spy in a really nice flow. Flowers just wasn't as good at that consistently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T04:11:12-07:00","id":185439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=182376#post182376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I totally understand how clever players could find ways to abuse this Exploit, but I also see ways that clever players can be, well, clever with it. I can imagine a demon who has spent a decade or more apprenticed to a mage, carefully pretending to be one of the Wise herself, and has access to a fairly huge range of spells as a result, and I can see the concept as either a horribly twinked out Sam Haight Special (in the worst cWoD sense) or a really nifty character with a complex Cover to maintain (especially as a bizarre antagonist). It's up to the player (and the ST) to determine whether the execution of that concept is awesome or just dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the book and I don't know the exact mechanics, but is there anything to keep this power from being an absolute spotlight stealer in crossover games? Just from this discussion I am getting horror visions of Demon with Celerity, Mage Armour and Garau form being better at their shtick than any other member of the party.<br /> In such a situation the demon doesn't care if the others notice that he is just faking the power (they know anyway) and most powers only need a single success anyway.<br /> The risk of attracting GM attention makes the problem <i>worse</i>. It answers the problem of one player having too much spotlight by putting them even more center stage. Forcing an additional actor into the scene that is specifically all about them does not help putting emphasis on the other characters. It's like the enemy flaw that many systems have that is secretly a bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T06:06:25-07:00","id":185459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185439#post185439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have the book and I don't know the exact mechanics, but is there anything to keep this power from being an absolute spotlight stealer in crossover games? Just from this discussion I am getting horror visions of Demon with Celerity, Mage Armour and Garau form being better at their shtick than any other member of the party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regular success will only ever give you one success on the standard effect. An exceptional success on the exploit gives you three successes. You can only mimic instant or reflexive powers, extended powers are verboten to you. It's contested by a pool of Wits + Supernatural Tolerance of the supernatural type you're mimicking. If you fail the roll, at all, in any way, any supernatural who is of the type of power that is being used knows exactly what's up. And every single use costs 1 Aether.<br /> <br /> It's an awesome ability, don't get me wrong (and hilariously versatile) but if you wanted ridiculous power, you'd be better off building around the Demon's own exploits, embeds and demonic form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T07:12:55-07:00","id":185494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185439#post185439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the book and I don't know the exact mechanics, but is there anything to keep this power from being an absolute spotlight stealer in crossover games? Just from this discussion I am getting horror visions of Demon with Celerity, Mage Armour and Garau form being better at their shtick than any other member of the party.<br /> In such a situation the demon doesn't care if the others notice that he is just faking the power (they know anyway) and most powers only need a single success anyway.<br /> The risk of attracting GM attention makes the problem <i>worse</i>. It answers the problem of one player having too much spotlight by putting them even more center stage. Forcing an additional actor into the scene that is specifically all about them does not help putting emphasis on the other characters. It's like the enemy flaw that many systems have that is secretly a bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>G-M attention is nothing to sneeze at, and saying bringing down hunter angels only makes the demon's player happier is a bit like saying a manifestation paradox is exactly what a mage's spotlight-hogging player wants. But leaving that aside:<br /> <br /> - Every use of another critter's power costs Aether. That's gonna run out quickly.<br /> - It only works on instant or reflexive activation powers (no extended actions).<br /> - It only does the bare minimum. Mages can accept penalties to make a spell bigger, last longer, affect more targets. Demons with Show of Power can't.<br /> - Aside from an exceptional success, you're treated as scoring 1 success no matter how many successes you get. Good luck outshining the Forces mage when you're doing...1 damage per turn to one target... On an exceptional success you are treated as having scored three successes.<br /> - Someone already mentioned the problem where having supernaturals of the same type around contests your Exploit roll, so the more badass the company you keep the less likely you are to successfully spoof their powers. &quot;Getting caught&quot; is really the least of your problems there.<br /> - Demon form is scary if you build it for an intended purpose. I'm not convinced that I can't one-up a Celerity + mage armor + Garau form if I picked the right form powers, and that would only require one compromise roll, not three.<br /> <br /> Show of Power is a strong power with a lot of utility, but it's the old &quot;jack of all trades, master of none&quot; shtick. Get the book. If you feel like the power is too good or too difficult to adjudicate for the crossover game you're running, don't allow it. It's mainly intended for straight Demon games, with some potential in crossover games where the demon might need to occasionally play &quot;assistant/backup X splat.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T11:12:18-07:00","id":185663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185494#post185494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Every use of another critter's power costs Aether. That's gonna run out quickly.<br /> - It only works on instant or reflexive activation powers (no extended actions).<br /> - It only does the bare minimum. Mages can accept penalties to make a spell bigger, last longer, affect more targets. Demons with Show of Power can't.<br /> - Aside from an exceptional success, you're treated as scoring 1 success no matter how many successes you get. Good luck outshining the Forces mage when you're doing...1 damage per turn to one target... On an exceptional success you are treated as having scored three successes.<br /> - Someone already mentioned the problem where having supernaturals of the same type around contests your Exploit roll, so the more badass the company you keep the less likely you are to successfully spoof their powers. &quot;Getting caught&quot; is really the least of your problems there.<br /> - Demon form is scary if you build it for an intended purpose. I'm not convinced that I can't one-up a Celerity + mage armor + Garau form if I picked the right form powers, and that would only require one compromise roll, not three.</div> </div> </div> </div>- So do many of the powers used by the mentioned supernaturals. And if the way the exploit works means that the the Demon can use an effect for one aether that would would cost a Mage/Vamp/whatever more than one Mana/Bp/whatever to use (like, say, a total of 2 mana for an improvised spell from a non-favoured arcana with a basecost of already one mana) the Demon <i>comes out ahead</i>. Ruling that the cost of the Exploit is basecost for a supernatural of that type +1 would fix that. So errata to make sure it costs 2 or 3 aether to emulate a power that costs 2 Bloodpoints/Glamout/Mana/etc.<br /> - Most of the powers I get visions of horror about are instant/reflexive<br /> - Being limited to one success effects means absolute jack in a system that's <i>based around never requiring more than one success</i>. Powers that require more than one success are the exception, not the rule, in NWoD. The problem isn't the Force's mage's direct damage spells that require extra successes (only dumb mages use that anyway), it's the demon looking at that forces mage with a grin and then transforming the entire bulding the BBEG is in into Nytroglycerin.<br /> Do Demons using the exploit apply all the dicemaluses the copied supernatural had to apply to their activation roll? Remember, NWoD uses dicemaluses for difficulty, not extra succeses. If the Demon sees a mage applying 10 to 15 dice of spell factors to create a spell, can they then copy that spell using their full dicepool or do they apply those same 10 or 15 dice as a malus?<br /> - So, if demon form is oh so badass, then what stops the Demon from combining their ultra-badass demon form with Celerity, mage armour and whatever else they can copy? Does the exploit not work while in Demon form? Who is one-upping who then?<br /> <br /> Edit: Example: The Demon sees a mage use an improvised, sympathetically cast transform earth with enhanced target factors that transforms a large area into acid. To cast the spell is an instant action and the mage pays at least 3 mana and gets a significant hit to their dicepool, but requires only one success. Is the Demon then able to copy that for the cheaper cost of one Aether, and using their full dicepool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 07-01-2014, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T11:16:12-07:00","id":185664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185663#post185663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Being limited to one success effects means absolute jack in a system that's <i>based around never requiring more than one success</i>. The problem isn't the Force's mage's direct damage spells that require extra successes (only dumb mages use that anyway), it's the demon looking at that forces mage with a grin and then transforming the entire bulding the BBEG is in into Nytroglycerin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requires the demon to have seen that effect in action and requires that range to be the base effect with no added factors. Meantime, have fun with your incredibly fragile and easily-counterspelled dupe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T11:30:22-07:00","id":185677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185664#post185664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requires the demon to have seen that effect in action and requires that range to be the base effect with no added factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey Mike, could you show me X effect with Y range and no added factor, so I can copy it next fight?&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure Elsa, here we go&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember, this is about mixed games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185664#post185664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meantime, have fun with your incredibly fragile and easily-counterspelled dupe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, waste a combat action counterspelling. Please do. Make my day.<br /> <br /> Alternatively: Counterspelling is hard when you are dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T14:32:39-07:00","id":185796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185664#post185664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requires the demon to have seen that effect in action and requires that range to be the base effect with no added factors. Meantime, have fun with your incredibly fragile and easily-counterspelled dupe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is important to keep in mind, Joker. The Mage can turn a large area into acid, but the Demon is probably gonna be able to make like... A cup of acid. Which he might not be able to throw because that stuff burns.<br /> <br /> Like seriously, maybe they can copy the effect but they can't copy the factors, and the factors are really the crazy stuff, as far as Mage is concerned. If they copy scary Vampire powers, I doubt they can get around limitations (Like the one Celerity interrupt per scene, for instance) and only rolling 1 success on your Dominate roll or whatever usually means anyone with supernatural tolerance and the sense to spend willpower could be looking at at least 4+ dice to beat your single success.<br /> <br /> Finally, there's really little stopping you from saying &quot;copying that effect is beyond the scope of your abilities, sorry.&quot; Which, given the whole spell factors schlub among other things, seems a perfectly equitable solution. Using direct damage spells is also silly since that'd be crazy inefficient and you'd be getting that 1 sux for them.<br /> <br /> As an aside, pretty sure every splat has strong prohibitions about revealing their natures to the uninitiated, and do you <i>really </i>want your demon &quot;friend&quot; who can switch faces, steal lives and annihilate souls to know every trick you've got up your sleeve? It's not the solution to the &quot;problem&quot; but an important consideration, too. If Mr. Stone kept asking to see that glamoury trick my vampire can do, I'd hesitate before showing him the same way I wouldn't want to teach a neonate who might use it on me. Etc.<br /> <br /> Really, I think disallowing them from emulating the spell factors solves the mage problem tidily. There may be a complaint, but nyuk, that's what happens when you've got a supercomputer for a soul rather than the whole Awakened shebang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-01-2014, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T14:37:15-07:00","id":185798,"title":"","content":"@Joker: The erata you describe is unnecessary, as that is how the power already works. Spell factors? Also addressed.<br /> <br /> Look, you seem to be kicking up a huge fuss largely out of assumptions made out of ignorance. I would suggest before you panic about the existence of this power that you read the text of the power in question. If you still have concerns that your players will abuse it, don't let it into your game.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, so apparently some of that wording was cut for space (I just got my contributor copy a couple days ago). That said, I agree that it's a good way to balance the power in crossover if you're concerned about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 07-01-2014, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T14:48:18-07:00","id":185804,"title":"","content":"I read all of this and find myself asking how we got here from a power that whose purpose is provide just enough to keep people from looking too deeply.<br /> <br /> If you're in a any sort of a confrontation that requires you to use a Exploit, eight out of ten times you're better off using something else and just lying your teeth off later-assuming angels don't bust up your party. Anything else, you use this and start praying&quot;Don't look at me, don't look at me&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-01-2014, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T15:14:36-07:00","id":185811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185798#post185798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Joker: The erata you describe is unnecessary, as that is how the power already works. Spell factors? Also addressed.<br /> <br /> Look, you seem to be kicking up a huge fuss largely out of assumptions made out of ignorance. I would suggest before you panic about the existance of this power that you read the text of the power in question. If you still have concerns that your players will abuse it, don't let it into your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, when I made my post I said that I didn't know how the power worked exactly. Which is why I asked. I actually missed the line about spell factors in your original post, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Also, three posts is a huge fuss now?<br /> <br /> <br /> But just to be sure I understand correctly, the cost of copying a power scales with the base cost of the copied power? No invoking third tier Utterances for the cost of one Aether?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T15:50:06-07:00","id":185823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185811#post185811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just to be sure I understand correctly, the cost of copying a power scales with the base cost of the copied power? No invoking third tier Utterances for the cost of one Aether?</div> </div> </div> </div>The cost is always one Aether. And to invoke that third tier utterance, you'd have to observe and survive it being used by that mummy. And of course you could only effectively use it when a Mummy wasn't present simply because Wits + Sehkem is going to be a huge contested pool - you can't forgo that contested pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T16:11:13-07:00","id":185831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185823#post185823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cost is always one Aether. And to invoke that third tier utterance, you'd have to observe and survive it being used by that mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned, this is about mixed games, so none of those two things are problems. You get ample chance to observe and getting rid of the contested pool is as hard as asking your friendly neighbourhood mummy to turn their back to you when you invoke the Utterance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 07-01-2014, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T17:05:23-07:00","id":185855,"title":"","content":"this might be getting too technical, but IIRC Mummies need to have a certain level of Sekhem to use third tier utterances. Show of Power only allows you to copy something as if you were [Primum] Supernatural Advantage creature, or something like that. I imagine for most Demons that, if that's the case, than Tier 3 Utterances are beyond the majority of Unchained, so it'll take a really high Primum Demon to take advantage of that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T21:28:38-07:00","id":185992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185831#post185831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned, this is about mixed games, so none of those two things are problems. You get ample chance to observe and getting rid of the contested pool is as hard as asking your friendly neighbourhood mummy to turn their back to you when you invoke the Utterance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rule says present, not observing. So turning your back still means that they're present at the scene - the only way that'd work is if they'd remove themselves from the scene and sit out participating. Not damn likely. And then of course, if you're mimicing a power from the supernatural you may be working against, if they're present they'll contest your pool as well. Plus this is going to shred your cover at an alarming rate if you're using that many exploits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">this might be getting too technical, but IIRC Mummies need to have a certain level of Sekhem to use third tier utterances. Show of Power only allows you to copy something as if you were [Primum] Supernatural Advantage creature, or something like that. I imagine for most Demons that, if that's the case, than Tier 3 Utterances are beyond the majority of Unchained, so it'll take a really high Primum Demon to take advantage of that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the Mummy rules, but the Demon rule is correct - the Demon using the power is assumed to have a native Powerstat = Primum for purposes of effects that use it for scaling/require it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T22:17:12-07:00","id":186038,"title":"","content":"It seems fairly clear to me that if you're in a cross-over game you're already walking through the thin veneer of game-balance anyway. If I'm not mistaken OPP haven't made any cross-over specific books, and <i>Flowers of Hell</i> certainly isn't one of them. The purpose of the power is to allow a demon to mimic a supernatural because when they assume a cover that is a vampire, they are not actually a vampire, but human and so if a vampire tries to determine if they are - they'd see a lovely beating heart and thus be very curious how it is that this supposed neonate is still <i>alive</i> and not among the undead. Show of Power allows the demon character to accurately mimic such qualities as a weakness to the sun, a lack of the blush of life or indeed the ability to consume human blood.<br /> <br /> More pertinent to this string of conversation is their ability to mimic instant and reflexive powers such as Celerity. Firstly: These powers are absolutely limited by that which the character encounters allowing the storyteller to limit exposure in order to maintain balance. Secondly, it will always call for a roll from observers - it says nothing about these observers having to be enemies of the character. Asking your friendly Mummy to turn his back is a bit suspicious... why do you need to turn your back, my supposedly Mummy friend, before you can reliably call your swarm of flesh eating scarab beetles? We've all seen it before, you needn't be bashful, I sent a swarm of flesh eating scarab beetles on a grumpy cultist just the other week!<br /> <br /> If the other player characters know that that character is a demon then there is a clear problem, isn't there? You've allowed that player to completely negate one of the number-one weaknesses of the demon template. <i>A demon must present themselves as someone else to avoid the God-Machine. </i>Therefore, if his demon friends are aware of his true nature, he has to have had at least one situation arise where he's had to roll Cover. If any of the supernatural observers are not aware, he must roll Cover again - even after already having to roll Cover for using the Exploit - because he is now behaving out-of-character for his Cover. The enemies count too. If he isn't acting in observance of what he is presenting, then it's a Cover roll, even if that creature doesn't necessarily know anymore about a demon than he does a mummy - the God-Machine knows.<br /> <br /> So it seems to me that it is less that the power needs balancing and more that you, the storyteller, must take the appropriate levels of due care when mixing supernaturals from separate splat books that were never designed to directly interact with one another. Can it be done? Yes. Should it be done? That's up to you. This is one of the hurdles you face. Another hurdle is you let a player play a mummy in a cross-over game. Those vampires are going to have a hard time living up to the ten plagues of Egypt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T01:22:50-07:00","id":186118,"title":"","content":"Excuse me, what is the value in point for a facade? 1 , 2 , 3 ? I dont read anything about the numeric value for the balance of the pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T01:47:18-07:00","id":186124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=185992#post185992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rule says present, not observing. So turning your back still means that they're present at the scene - the only way that'd work is if they'd remove themselves from the scene and sit out participating. Not damn likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the way it's written that's better. I was going of the quote in the other thread which is &quot;vs. highest Wits + Supernatural Tolerance of observers of emulated supernatural type&quot; for the contested pool. Not counting as an observer is much easier than not counting as present.<br /> <br /> My main problems are that the Demon doesn't apply the same penalties a creature of that type does (though going by Eric's comment he intended for them to and it was just edited out) and that the cost doesn't scale. Which means a Demon can end up being able to do another supernatural creatures tricks cheaper and with a higher base dicepool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T02:02:07-07:00","id":186128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=186038#post186038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More pertinent to this string of conversation is their ability to mimic instant and reflexive powers such as Celerity. Firstly: These powers are absolutely limited by that which the character encounters allowing the storyteller to limit exposure in order to maintain balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>If allowing a power into a game means the ST suddenly has to be very careful about which enemies they use and has to invest lots of extra work and attention and fixing the problems they only noticed too late, that does not speak well of the power!<br /> &quot;Here is cool power, but if you want to include it you'll have to rework two thirds of the NSCs you prepared or it will wreck gamebalance. Oh, and better not use supernatural type X at all, so redo that whole campaign story if you still want to allow the exploit. And we will not tell you about all these problems in the book, so better hope you are reading our forums or you will not know beforehand&quot;.<br /> That's not the sign of a good power. If including it means that the ST might get into the situation of having to ask one of their players to have their Demon forget they witnessed power Y for the sake of balance that is also not good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T07:25:26-07:00","id":186291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=186128#post186128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If allowing a power into a game means the ST suddenly has to be very careful about which enemies they use and has to invest lots of extra work and attention and fixing the problems they only noticed too late, that does not speak well of the power!<br /> &quot;Here is cool power, but if you want to include it you'll have to rework two thirds of the NSCs you prepared or it will wreck gamebalance. Oh, and better not use supernatural type X at all, so redo that whole campaign story if you still want to allow the exploit. And we will not tell you about all these problems in the book, so better hope you are reading our forums or you will not know beforehand&quot;.<br /> That's not the sign of a good power. If including it means that the ST might get into the situation of having to ask one of their players to have their Demon forget they witnessed power Y for the sake of balance that is also not good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where I see a power that lets a demon go undercover as another type of supernatural being, biting his nails every step of the way but able to pull it off, you see a game-breaking Sam Haight Special that your players will use to make your game unfun. That's okay. I've been GMing for more than 25 years, and I've banned or houseruled my fair share of powers.<br /> <br /> I suggest checking out some of the many other Embeds, Exploits, and demon form powers that Flowers of Hell has to offer. Apple of Discord has been called out as a fun Cacophony Embed, Associate and Integrate as Mundane, and Demon Car as a nifty (if particularly audacious) Exploit. I'm personally fond of Play Possum, Call Out, Like the Movies, and Open and Shut Case. Strength Through Adversity is just fun and evil, and I can think of a zillion in-genre ways to use the Aquatic Propulsion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T07:31:16-07:00","id":186292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=186118#post186118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me, what is the value in point for a facade? 1 , 2 , 3 ? I dont read anything about the numeric value for the balance of the pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same a cover pact, and thus you get and apply the same amount of cover exp to the facade. It's just not permanent.<br /> <br /> In other words, it's about how much you can wrangle out of a dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T08:24:00-07:00","id":186304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=186291#post186291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest checking out some of the many other Embeds, Exploits, and demon form powers that Flowers of Hell has to offer. Apple of Discord has been called out as a fun Cacophony Embed, Associate and Integrate as Mundane, and Demon Car as a nifty (if particularly audacious) Exploit. I'm personally fond of Play Possum, Call Out, Like the Movies, and Open and Shut Case. Strength Through Adversity is just fun and evil, and I can think of a zillion in-genre ways to use the Aquatic Propulsion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, High of Birth feeds in nicely to my weird newfound obsession with Sleeve Integrators.<br /> <br /> That reminds me: does a demon possessing a Sleeve Integrator gain access to any Supernatural Merits the stigmatic had?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-02-2014, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T13:42:03-07:00","id":186486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=186292#post186292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the same a cover pact, and thus you get and apply the same amount of cover exp to the facade. It's just not permanent.<br /> <br /> In other words, it's about how much you can wrangle out of a dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the max value of the cover is set to One... so, i need 3 px for make a cover 1 facade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T14:44:19-07:00","id":186524,"title":"","content":"Can password entropy be used to figure out the proper response coded exchanges to confirm who's who or similar? Could it also be used for figuring out activation criteria for activating magic items? Also if it applies to the first one it really serves to ratchet up the paranoia for Demons because you can't set up a protocol to confirm it's actually your buddy in that new Cover you've never seen before short of going for full on demonic form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1965-joebobjoe","name":"joebobjoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T15:20:49-07:00","id":186548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=186486#post186486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the max value of the cover is set to One... so, i need 3 px for make a cover 1 facade?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Any</i> Cover Pact, ostensibly, seeing as a Fa\u00e7ade is <i>more</i> fragile than a Cover 1 patch job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T15:46:02-07:00","id":186568,"title":"","content":"Good point! Thanks Satchel! Thanks to Arcane Arts too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T00:32:00-07:00","id":187763,"title":"","content":"This was several pages back, but; the answer to dealing with sunk willpower costs for gadgets is to treat the XP value like the sanctity of merits rule. Lose the gadget, get your XP back. This is often a taste issue. I absolutely hate spending XP on perishable resources and avoid it whenever possible. One of my best gamer friends never makes those house rules when she's the storyteller because she thinks sanctity rules are ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:50:36-07:00","id":189560,"title":"","content":"I really hope this hits PoD soon. It's sounds like such a good book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:24:08-07:00","id":194023,"title":"","content":"I have really enjoyed this book. I must say the information on the command and control infrastructure provided a very dark, for me, viewpoint/interpretation on the God-Machine, namely that there is no sentient entity behind the God-Machine. Just a network of interlinked and networked decision centers, with no more of an emergent super-mind than offices in a bureaucracy. A set of unaware interacting rules, whose original &quot;seed&quot; and purpose could have long since perished. Very creepy to think something like that is a major player in the material world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:26:30-07:00","id":194025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/179990-flowers-of-hell-discussion-thread?p=194023#post194023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have really enjoyed this book. I must say the information on the command and control infrastructure provided a very dark, for me, viewpoint/interpretation on the God-Machine, namely that there is no sentient entity behind the God-Machine. Just a network of interlinked and networked decision centers, with no more of an emergent super-mind than offices in a bureaucracy. A set of unaware interacting rules, whose original &quot;seed&quot; and purpose could have long since perished. Very creepy to think something like that is a major player in the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The creepiest thing is that, if you remove the mecha-angels and the dalgas and the magic workings that produce supernatural output, you have just described the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T01:06:29-07:00","id":194422,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> True, I didn't cop that when I wrote it. Would be cool if the laws of physics in the real world could summon mecha-angels!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T14:48:58-07:00","id":240767,"title":"","content":"I got my discount for the Flowers of Hell PoD today!<br /> <br /> Which means print fans can buy their copies now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T20:56:46-07:00","id":241029,"title":"","content":"And I so would buy it, right now. Today, this very instant. If it weren't for my preference of purchasing all my books in lots. So, I guess I play the waiting game until Seattle and Fiction hits PoD. Oh well, I'm glad it's here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","